{% comment %}
Configure up to ten EasyStore product-handle limits.
Leave a handle blank to disable that slot. Handles are normalized to lowercase at runtime.

Refresh timestamps renew an allowance. Once a refresh timestamp has passed, orders
placed before it stop counting, so every customer starts the limit again from zero.
A timestamp in the future changes nothing until it arrives.

Write timestamps with the store's timezone offset, for example
'2026-09-01 00:00:00 +0800'. A slot with a blank refresh falls back to
customer_order_limit_refresh_all, and when that is blank too every past order
keeps counting forever.
{% endcomment %}
